    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on August 29th, our offensive engine is centered on high-efficiency, speed-centric profiles. **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) and **Corbin Carroll** (71.85) headline today\u2019s starters, benefiting from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Seiya Suzuki** is our top play, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Abbott, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start; his ability to impact the SB category\u2014which we continue to overweigh\u2014makes him a cornerstone despite a park factor slightly draggy for his profile. **Brice Turang** (70.37) is the efficiency king today, climbing above 70 thanks to a perfect storm: the leadoff spot and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor against Quantrill that effectively guarantees the green light for our stolen base hunt.\n\nElsewhere, the volatility of the back-end spots remains a focal point. **Josh Naylor** (66.82) is a mandatory start against Soriano, but we are monitoring the bottom of the order closely. **Austin Riley** (61.87) provides surprising value at the #8 spot due to his high raw power and a favorable matchup against Agnos, while **Gabriel Moreno** (62.88) continues to outperform expectations as a high-floor catcher against a struggling Wilkinson. Our most difficult decision occurred at the fringe of the bench, where **Griffin Conine** (43.60) narrowly missed the cut. While **Griffin Conine** holds platoon upside, the optimizer penalized his projected output against the high-velocity, elite-arm profile of Cavalli, leading us to favor the relative consistency of **Max Muncy** (56.30) and his park-adjusted upside against Baz. \n\nWe are currently navigating a depleted depth chart, with **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** all unavailable due to IL status or benching. As we chase the 5x5 categories, keep an eye on **Jose Caballero** (58.65); his efficiency is dampened by the #9 slot, but his game-changing speed potential keeps him firmly in the mix. With no extreme weather flags reported, our focus remains on maximizing plate appearances from the top four slots, specifically relying on **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll** to secure the steals necessary to maintain our competitive edge in this Roto format.",
